{"explanation":"The law of cosines says c² = a² + b² − 2ab·cos(C). The first part, a² + b², is exactly the Pythagorean theorem. The extra term −2ab·cos(C) is the correction for the angle not being 90°. When C = 90°, cos C = 0 and the correction vanishes. When C is acute, the correction is positive, so c is shorter than the right-triangle value. When C is obtuse, the correction is negative, so c is longer. Drag the vertex or use the slider to change C and watch the correction term and the sides change.","manimCode":"const a = 2.2, b = 2.8;
const origin = [-2.5, -1.5, 0];
let C = Math.PI / 2;

const title = new MathTex({ latex: 'c^2 = a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\\cos C' });
await title.waitForRender();
title.moveTo([0, 3.2, 0]);
scene.add(title);

// Vertex C at origin, side b along x axis, side a at angle C
const ptC = origin;
const ptB = [origin[0] + b, origin[1], 0];
function ptA(ang) { return [origin[0] + a * Math.cos(ang), origin[1] + a * Math.sin(ang), 0]; }

const tri = new Polygon({ vertices: [ptC, ptB, ptA(C)], color: WHITE });
tri.setFill(BLUE_E, 0.4);
const dotA = new Dot({ point: ptA(C), color: YELLOW });
scene.add(tri, dotA);

let info = null;
function updateInfo() {
  if (info) scene.remove(info);
  const deg = C * 180 / Math.PI;
  const pyth = a * a + b * b;
  const corr = -2 * a * b * Math.cos(C);
  const c2 = pyth + corr;
  const lines = [
    'C = ' + deg.toFixed(0) + ' deg',
    'a^2 + b^2 = ' + pyth.toFixed(2),
    'correction = ' + corr.toFixed(2),
    'c^2 = ' + c2.toFixed(2)
  ].join('\n');
  info = new Text({ text: lines, color: corr > 0.01 ? RED : (corr < -0.01 ? GREEN : YELLOW), fontSize: 26 });
  info.moveTo([3.5, 0, 0]);
  scene.add(info);
}

function setAngle(ang) {
  C = ang;
  const p = ptA(C);
  dotA.moveTo(p);
  tri.setVertices([ptC, ptB, p]);
  updateInfo();
}
updateInfo();

makeDraggable(dotA, scene, {
  onDrag: () => {
    const [x, y] = dotA.getCenter();
    let ang = Math.atan2(y - origin[1], x - origin[0]);
    ang = Math.max(0.1, Math.min(Math.PI - 0.1, ang));
    C = ang;
    const p = ptA(C);
    dotA.moveTo(p);
    tri.setVertices([ptC, ptB, p]);
    updateInfo();
  }
});

const controls = new Controls(scene, { position: 'top-right' });
controls.addSlider({ label: 'Angle C (rad)', min: 0.1, max: 3.04, value: Math.PI / 2, step: 0.02, onChange: (v) => setAngle(v) });
controls.addButton({ label: 'Set C = 90 deg', onClick: () => setAngle(Math.PI / 2) });

await scene.wait(999999);"}

